{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"## Context / Problem\nThe three provider overlays contain repeated or historical comments identified by the audit and revalidated on `origin/main` at `0033662b5534531d84e39d4a14bf75c8e768e85e`. Shortening them must preserve provider selection, cross-provider comparability, and credential isolation.\n\n## Approach\nEdit only standalone comments and blank lines in the declared TOML files. Preserve configuration values byte-for-byte and retain the minimum current rationale needed by external-test operators.\n\n## Scope\n- `anthropic.toml` — Preserve explicit config-file-path coverage, credential name, provider-qualified `[llm] model`, and all three model-class slots so ambient provider defaults cannot leak in.\n- `bedrock.toml` — Preserve same-Claude-family cross-provider comparability; inference-profile-only IDs with nonuniform suffixes; verbatim AWS discovery; region and ambient-AWS credentials; provider-qualified scalar model plus every class slot; and matrix-only Anthropic-key blanking.\n- `openai.toml` — Preserve best-effort support tier, credential, verified models, provider-qualified scalar model, and every class slot.\n\nConsumers are `src/rebar/_config_sources.py` plus the LLM config/class resolver; `.github/workflows/external-integration.yml`; `.github/workflows/structured-output-baseline.yml`; `.github/workflows/jira-dc-richtext-probe.yml` for the Anthropic overlay; the `rebar.toml` and Compose Bedrock pins; and provider/config pin tests. Workflow prose is owned by `sphalerite-bereft-tortoise`; the stale provider README is tracked by `wearied-convincing-arrowana`.\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] The one-commit changed-path set is exactly the 3-path file-impact set.\n- [ ] Only ordinary comments and adjacent blank lines change.\n- [ ] Every TOML configuration value remains byte-identical.\n- [ ] Every behavior-bearing directive remains byte-identical.\n- [ ] Every Scope constraint has a non-author `semantic-preservation=PASS` row with immutable before/final citations.\n- [ ] Every consumer contract has a non-author `semantic-preservation=PASS` row with immutable before/final citations.\n- [ ] Every edited prose block has a non-author `bloat-removal=PASS` row.\n- [ ] Every required semantic-review row is present.\n- [ ] Every recorded focused check exits 0 at the leaf commit.\n- [ ] The recorded path-scoped `git diff --check` exits 0 at the leaf commit.\n- [ ] The recorded worktree-venv lint command exits 0 at the leaf commit.\n\n## Verification\nRun the recorded content-only guards, focused checks, path-scoped diff check, and worktree-venv lint. The independent matrix, not exact prose matching, judges semantic preservation."}},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1788667507796760001,"uuid":"af385d39-f1da-4bf3-9cdc-c166f3ebd589"}